==English==
{{was wotd|2009|May|1}}
[[Image:Belgian barquentine Mercator. Trinidad, c. 1960.jpg|thumb|350px|The Belgian barquentine ''Mercator'' shown here has three masts: a square-rigged foremast on the left, a fore-and-aft-rigged mainmast in the middle, and a fore-and-aft-rigged '''mizzenmast''' on the right.]]

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|mizzen-mast|mizenmast}}

===Etymology===
{{compound|en|mizzen|mast}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/ˈmɪz.ənˌmɑːst/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|/ˈmɪz.ənˌmæst/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-mizzenmast.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|nautical}} The [[aftmost]] [[mast]] on a ship having three or more masts; the third-tallest mast on a [[full-rigged]] ship.
# {{lb|en|nautical}} The second mast of a ship having two masts where the second one is shorter, such as a [[ketch]] or [[yawl]].

